    {
      "id": 205069,
      "name": "jorgenp",
      "username": "jorgenp",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/958977/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-09-29T21:04:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've always speculated that it would be Final Wasteland or Magmaria.&nbsp; I could also see Silver Gulch being it, bizarrely.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The environments have been extremes related to the core factors that drive the hero.&nbsp; Argent Adept had the extremes of nature in Insula Primalis.&nbsp; Captain Cosmic went to the extreme ends of the universe ending up in the Enclave of the Endlings.&nbsp; Tempest's extreme is a representation of his refugee status, with Dok'thorath being the homeworld of the tyrant that destroyed Tempest's home planet.&nbsp; Fanatic in the Court of Blood is, of course, an extreme of religion.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thus we need to look into the extremes for Haka, the eternal warrior who wanders the Earth.&nbsp; The Final Wasteland would be representing the extreme of eternity, but we've already had that environment used for another Haka unlock, so I kind of doubt it.&nbsp; Magmaria on the other hand, certainly counts as an extreme environment, and this would be representing Haka's exploration of Earth; you don't get much more extreme than the core of the planet.&nbsp; Silver Gulch would be an extreme of time, but I feel it is certainly the weakest concept of the three.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So yeah, I'm rooting for Magmaria.&nbsp; My guess for the actual effect is something regarding Savage Mana, but I guess we'll see...</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:34:19.841Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
