      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I&#39;ve always speculated that it would be Final Wasteland or Magmaria.&nbsp; I could also see Silver Gulch being it, bizarrely.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The environments have been extremes related to the core factors that drive the hero.&nbsp; Argent Adept had the extremes of nature in Insula Primalis.&nbsp; Captain Cosmic went to the extreme ends of the universe ending up in the Enclave of the Endlings.&nbsp; Tempest&#39;s extreme is a representation of his refugee status, with Dok&#39;thorath being the homeworld of the tyrant that destroyed Tempest&#39;s home planet.&nbsp; Fanatic in the Court of Blood is, of course, an extreme of religion.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thus we need to look into the extremes for Haka, the eternal warrior who wanders the Earth.&nbsp; The Final Wasteland would be representing the extreme of eternity, but we&#39;ve already had that environment used for another Haka unlock, so I kind of doubt it.&nbsp; Magmaria on the other hand, certainly counts as an extreme environment, and this would be representing Haka&#39;s exploration of Earth; you don&#39;t get much more extreme than the core of the planet.&nbsp; Silver Gulch would be an extreme of time, but I feel it is certainly the weakest concept of the three.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So yeah, I&#39;m rooting for Magmaria.&nbsp; My guess for the actual effect is something regarding Savage Mana, but I guess we&#39;ll see...</p>",
